{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Cf5kXwUw24K1qvoj1Zmkq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** — Add a new ErrorCode value `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM` to represent the case where a shipment in CANCELLED status cannot be confirmed (409 Conflict). This follows the existing pattern where specific codes describe why an operation failed.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** — Add a new endpoint `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` that:\n   - Fetches the shipment by ID (throw 404 if not found)\n   - Checks the shipment's current status:\n     - If `CREATED`: update status to `CONFIRMED`, save, and return with 200 OK\n     - If `CONFIRMED`: return as-is with 200 OK (idempotent, no state change)\n     - If `CANCELLED`: throw `ConflictException` with code `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM` (409)\n   - Returns the shipment in the response body\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Add four new test cases:\n   - `confirms a CREATED shipment to CONFIRMED` — verifies status change and persistence\n   - `idempotently confirms an already CONFIRMED shipment` — verifies retry succeeds with no change\n   - `rejects confirming a CANCELLED shipment with 409` — verifies the error code\n   - `reports unknown shipment on confirm` — verifies 404 when shipment doesn't exist\n\n**Alternative rejected:**\n\nI considered putting confirmation logic in a separate service class, but the existing architecture has controllers calling repositories directly (see OrderController, which also handles business logic inline). This is consistent with the simple Spring Boot architecture already established.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Input | Logic | Output | HTTP Status |\n|------|-------|-------|--------|------------|\n| CREATED → CONFIRMED | shipmentId for CREATED shipment | Read shipment, update status field, save back | Shipment with CONFIRMED status | 200 OK |\n| CONFIRMED → CONFIRMED | shipmentId for CONFIRMED shipment | Read shipment, no update, return as-is | Shipment unchanged | 200 OK |\n| CANCELLED | shipmentId for CANCELLED shipment | Read shipment, check status, throw ConflictException | ApiError with SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM | 409 Conflict |\n| Not found | nonexistent shipmentId | findById returns null, throw ResourceNotFoundException | ApiError with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND | 404 Not Found |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. Test case: \"confirms a CREATED shipment\" — creates shipment, confirms it, verifies status changed to CONFIRMED\n2. Test case: \"idempotently confirms a CONFIRMED shipment\" — creates, confirms, confirms again, verifies second succeeds and no error\n3. Test case: \"rejects confirming a CANCELLED shipment\" — manually saves a CANCELLED shipment to repository, tries to confirm, verifies 409 with SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM code\n4. Test case: \"reports unknown shipment on confirm\" — confirms nonexistent ID, verifies 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND code\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nLet me implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1606,"cache_read_input_tokens":16844,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1606},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d8c4e419-987f-41ee-a0da-06e5b5ff9fcf","uuid":"93d65307-fa23-42aa-be42-ab97fda525da","timestamp":"2026-09-15T19:08:53.383Z","request_id":"req_011Cf5kXw3dKA5XvwmADhgcQ"}
